# infra/foundation — slipway platform `<% name %>` (<% environment %>)

Generated by `platform.cjs` from `platform.yaml`. Owns the organisation's <%#if azure.registry.existing%>role assignments on the existing registry `<% azure.registry.name %>`<%else%>registry `<% azure.registry.name %>`<%/if%>, key vault `<% azure.key_vault_name %>`, Container Apps environment `<% azure.container_app_environment %>`, Log Analytics `<% azure.log_analytics_name %>`<%#if azure.shared_apps_identity%>, the optional shared apps identity `<% derived.apps_identity_name %>`<%/if%>. The resource group, the state storage and the CI/CD identity `<% azure.cicd_identity_name %>` come from `setup-platform.sh`.

| Step | Who | Command |
|---|---|---|
| Plan | anyone with Reader on the subscription | `export ARM_SUBSCRIPTION_ID=$(az account show --query id -o tsv); terraform -chdir=infra/foundation init && terraform -chdir=infra/foundation plan -out=tfplan.<% environment %>` |
| Apply | the platform owner, after reading the plan | `terraform -chdir=infra/foundation apply tfplan.<% environment %>` |
| Conditioned grants for per-app identities (after the apply) | a subscription **Owner** | `bash setup-platform.sh --grant-per-app-roles` |

State: `<% azure.state.storage_account %>/<% azure.state.container %>/<% name %>/platform/<% environment %>.tfstate` (Entra ID auth). Never `-auto-approve`, never `destroy`: repositories of the whole organisation depend on these resources.
